<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-of-ace-inhibitors-or-arbs-to-slow-kidney-damage-in-diabetic-kidney-disease> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use of ACE Inhibitors or ARBs to Slow Kidney Damage in Diabetic Kidney Disease" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes who have high blood pressure and DKD" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-of-ace-inhibitors-or-arbs-to-slow-kidney-damage-in-diabetic-kidney-disease" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Two types of blood pressure medicines, ACE inhibitors and ARBs, play a special role in protecting your kidneys. Each has been found to slow kidney damage in people with diabetes who have high blood pressure and DKD. The names of these medicines end in –pril or –sartan. ACE inhibitors and ARBs are not safe for women who are pregnant." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Two types of blood pressure medicines, ACE inhibitors and ARBs, play a special role in protecting your kidneys. Each has been found to slow kidney damage in people with diabetes who have high blood pressure and DKD. The names of these medicines end in –pril or –sartan. ACE inhibitors and ARBs are not safe for women who are pregnant." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-diabetic-kidney-disease> .

